# Protocol baseline
#
# The upstream snapshot this client implementation is written against. Every
# protocol-layer change must be traceable to the version recorded here.
# Drift detection (scripts/drift-check.sh) reads this file.

UPSTREAM_REPO=NodePassProject/Nowhere
UPSTREAM_BRANCH=main
UPSTREAM_TAG=v1.8.2
UPSTREAM_COMMIT=8807960c
UPSTREAM_COMMIT_DATE=2026-08-26
BINARY_VERSION_STRING=nowhere-v1.8.2

# Normative files watched for change
SPEC_FILES=docs/protocol.md docs/configuration.md docs/compatibility.md docs/security.md

# Known state
# - Advanced from v1.8.0 to v1.8.2 on 2026-08-26, on the first normative change
#   the drift check has ever reported. What changed, in full:
#     * TLS Mux shard density 12 -> 4 active flows before another shard opens
#       (protocol.md section 7, compatibility.md, configuration.md, operations.md);
#     * the default NOW_QUIC_MEMORY_PROFILE moved from `balanced` to `throughput`,
#       which is a Portal-side environment default with no client-visible effect.
#   Both are runtime tuning. No wire field, frame layout, length, ordering or
#   derivation changed anywhere: the diff over 4 commits touches one Rust
#   constant, one env default, their tests, and the prose that quotes them.
#   Every byte-level vector in this suite is unaffected, and re-running
#   verify-vectors.py after the transcription fix confirms it.
# - Sharding is client-side placement (protocol.md: "Sharding is runtime placement
#   and does not add wire fields"), so a client using the old density would still
#   interoperate. It is transcribed anyway because D-08 says this client follows
#   upstream, and because L2 is where the number gets read.
# - Relative to 1.8.0: no change to authentication (section 2), FlowHeader
#   (section 4), Target (section 5), SetupResult, UoT, MuxHeader or the QUIC
#   DATAGRAM header. The 59-vector fixture carries across unchanged.
# - Relative to 1.7: adds the TLS Mux carrier; removes the pool parameter
#   (replaced by mux=0|1, default 0); drops the Linux-only gate and adds
#   cross-platform CI plus GHCR container images.
# - Verified at v1.8.2: cargo build --release --locked succeeds on macOS/aarch64,
#   and the end-to-end smoke test passes against the resulting binary.
#
# Tracking policy (decided 2026-08-24, applied 2026-08-26)
#
# The baseline is NOT advanced just because upstream moved: a moving target
# during the first implementation of the protocol layer costs more than it buys,
# and the vectors in this suite were derived against a specific snapshot. Only a
# normative change - one of the SPEC_FILES above - interrupts development, and
# drift-check.sh exits non-zero so a scheduled CI job can open an issue.
#
# The steady state is therefore: upstream ahead, drift-check reporting the
# distance and passing.
#
# The 2026-08-26 advance is what that policy asks for on a normative change: read
# the diff, decide whether it reaches the wire, and only then move the pin. It
# reached two constants and no bytes, so moving the pin cost a rebuild of the
# host-side oracle and a one-line transcription fix. Had it reached the wire, the
# answer would have been to hold the pin and schedule the work.
#
# Revisit again at the L1 exit, or immediately on the next normative change.
#
# When advancing the baseline: run scripts/drift-check.sh first, then update this
# file, then re-run scripts/verify-vectors.py and scripts/smoke-local.sh.
